From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 04:12:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: piano: Assign active-low WAKE# to WLAN

GPIO104 is the dedicated active-low PEACH WAKE# line. Describing it
on the PCIe root port lets it wake the system even when WLAN wake
is disabled. Move the GPIO to the fixed WLAN endpoint so PCI uses
the WLAN device wake policy. The active-low polarity matches the
board wiring and Qualcomm's correction for the same signal.

Codex checked the board DTBs and combined the polarity correction
with the move. GPIO104 did not end the unplugged RTC suspend test
early on the Piano development image.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=eec036783b2e633302bcf277ae36742dfd3402fc
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts
index 9312b3e3c..0fc4ed6d5 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8750-xiaomi-piano.dts
@@ -1367,12 +1367,12 @@
 };
 
 &pcieport0 {
-	wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 102 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 	wifi@0 {
 		compatible = "pci17cb,110e";
 		reg = <0x10000 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x0>;
+		wake-gpios = <&tlmm 104 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 
 		vddrfacmn-supply = <&vreg_pmu_rfa_cmn>;
 		vddaon-supply = <&vreg_pmu_aon_0p59>;
-- 
